\details{
The class of evidence of a link is the coarsest taxonomic generalisation
needed by its best supporting record. For each record, each side gets the
finest rank shared by the node and the taxon of the record (\code{"exact"} when
the record names the node or one of its aliases, then \code{"genus"},
\code{"subfamily"}, \code{"family"}, \code{"order"}, \code{"class"}); a record of a generic
resource group (such as "Algae") gets \code{"generic"}, and a record that
shares no rank up to class with the node (only through surrogates) gets
\code{"beyond"}. The record's class is the coarser of its two sides and the
link takes the finest class among its records. Links that rely on a
surrogate sharing no rank with the node are marked \code{extrapolated} and
treated as \code{"class"} by \code{\link[=sample_metawebs]{sample_metawebs()}}. Manual links have class
\code{"manual"}.
}
\section{Missing values and zeros}{

A pair of nodes without any matching record has no link: as in WebBuilder,
absence of a record is treated as absence of the link. \code{\link[=calibrate_links]{calibrate_links()}}
explains why the probability of such pairs is not modelled.
}

